# Exact source and prior-report audit

1. Serge Tabachnikov, *A Baker's Dozen of Problems*, Arnold Mathematical Journal1(2015),59–67, Section7, printed p.62. The original HTML labels it Problem4; the full publisher PDF gives the same paragraph. It asks for parameter conditions for alternating null chains on the analytic Minkowski ellipsoid and motivates the question by Cayley's classical formula. It does not explicitly require a determinant or polynomial equation. Full original PDF and HTML were read for this item. [HTML](https://amj.math.stonybrook.edu/html-articles/Files-2015-2024/14-01/); [publisher PDF](https://amj.math.stonybrook.edu/pdf-Springer-final/014-0001-3.pdf).
2. Daniel Genin, Boris Khesin and Serge Tabachnikov, *Geodesics on an ellipsoid in Minkowski space*, Enseign. Math.(2)53(2007),307–331; [arXiv:0705.0188v1](https://arxiv.org/abs/0705.0188). Full primary preprint obtained; Sections1–5 and the relevant null-direction, confocal, tropic and invariant-density arguments were read. Theorem5.1 proves the Poncelet theorem for the folded equator map, and Problem5.2 asks for its parameter condition. The inspected source assumes a>b in its general-position analysis. The direct coordinates in this attempt cover every positive a,b,c, including a=b.
3. Gisbert Wüstholz, *Periods & billiards on the triaxial ellipsoid*, Halong workshop,24June2017. [Full primary slides](https://viasm.edu.vn/Cms_Data/Contents/viasm/Media/file/billards_halong2017.pdf). The last null-geodesic slides explicitly refer to Tabachnikov's problem and announce a number-field arithmetic criterion involving additional Jacobian loci. This is a slide announcement, not a full proof recovered in this audit. No equivalence to the present parameter-integral formula or the imported division-polynomial claim is inferred.

A bounded current search checked the exact target, null-geodesic chain and closure terminology, and the announced Wüstholz work. It found no verified available full algebraic characterization for every prescribed chain type. This search is not a proof of novelty or of continued openness of every formulation. Results for ambient billiards inside ellipsoids, Minkowski-plane conics and a hyperboloid surface have distinct phase spaces and are not substituted for this target.

The imported report is preserved unchanged in prior_imported_report.json. Its real invariant-coordinate translation is credited to GKT. Its assertion that the associated meromorphic differential is of the second kind, and that Abel's theorem automatically supplies an ordinary elliptic-group translation and division-polynomial test, is not accepted. Section5 of the new artifact gives the direct pole/residue check identifying the differential as third kind and the precise missing inference.

Before new proof work, the current queued0/5 row, full pinned record and full imported report, all-ref selected-path history, remote branch lookup,96 all-state PRs and related-target/state metadata were checked. No prior Alec/campaign attempt or duplicate was found. Dataset600008 is unique for these ellipsoid chains. The other null-geodesic record20002036 concerns spin lifts and parity on Lorentzian tori and is distinct. The adjacent future arborescence work is unrelated.
